<title>UK: UK govt to answer questions on tunnel fire.</title>
<headline>UK govt to answer questions on tunnel fire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Transport Secretary Sir George Young will answer emergency questions in parliament at 1530 GMT on the fire that swept through the channel tunnel overnight, the Department of Transport said.</p>
<p>Eurotunnel, the Anglo-French operator of the tunnel, earlier told Reuters its traffic would be cut to one third of normal levels by the fire, which seriously injured two people. It gave no indication of when normal traffic would resume.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44-171-542 7767</p>
